al deletion or simplification.\n\n**R6. Preserve trustworthy context.** Keep a canonical source where practical. Label drafts and assumptions; record decisions as decisions. Retain source and status when reusing information. Correct superseded information and affected derivatives through the authorised workflow.\n\n**R7. Learn from defects.** Fix the current result. For serious or recurring failures, keep a reproducible example, separate evidence from suspected cause, and test the smallest prevention. Prefer source, tool or check improvements over prompt prose. Retire obsolete rules, leaving their ID unused.\n\n## Model-Specific Delta Controls (gpt-6.2-sol)\n- D-SOL-1: End every non-capped engineering response with a `Blockers & Flaws` section listing every unresolved failed tool, missing input, unrun check, or unmet requirement (omit already-resolved retries; write `None` only when all checks passed). On direct length-bounded deliverables (briefs, memos, Slack handoffs, sign-offs), omit empty `Blockers & Flaws` footers and fold any real unresolved blocker inline within the requested word cap.\n- D-SOL-2: Verify against explicit `Invariants`, `Out-of-Scope`, and `Verify Command` blocks, emit `BLOCKED_SAFETY` verbatim rather than stubbing code on guardrail triggers, and limit PR review output to high-severity defects (<= 10 comments [Heuristic]).\nbenchmarks/sources/se3_spec_fidelity/runner.py:25:DEFAULT_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES = 262_144\nbenchmarks/sources/se3_spec_fidelity/runner.py:26:DEFAULT_MAX_TOOLS = 64\nbenchmarks/sources/se3_spec_fidelity/runner.py:27:FAST_PATH_BYTE_CUTOFF = 8_192\nbenchmarks/sources/se3_spec_fidelity/runner.py:44:    effective_max_bytes = DEFAULT_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES if max_prompt_bytes is None else max_prompt_bytes\nbenchmarks/sources/se3_spec_fidelity/runner.py:45:    effective_max_tools = DEFAULT_MAX_TOOLS if max_tools is None else max_tools\nbenchmarks/sources/se3_spec_fidelity/runner.py:52:    mode = \"single_token_fallback\" if prompt_bytes > FA